{title: When the Saints Go Marching In}
{artist: Traditional spiritual}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 120}
{tag: Easy}
{tag: Singalong}
{meta: language en}

{comment: Three chords and everybody already knows the words. A good one to start an evening with.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Oh when the [C]saints go marching in
Oh when the saints go marching [G7]in
Oh [C]how I want to [C7]be in that [F]number
When the [C]saints go [G7]marching [C]in
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Oh when the [C]sun refuse to shine
Oh when the sun refuse to [G7]shine
Oh [C]how I want to [C7]be in that [F]number
When the [C]sun re[G7]fuse to [C]shine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Oh when the [C]new world is revealed
Oh when the new world is re[G7]vealed
Oh [C]how I want to [C7]be in that [F]number
When the [C]new world [G7]is re[C]vealed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Oh when the [C]trumpet sounds its call
Oh when the trumpet sounds its [G7]call
Oh [C]how I want to [C7]be in that [F]number
When the [C]trumpet [G7]sounds its [C]call
{end_of_verse}
